trajectory.patch:
`test_out_of_bounds` is failing because the `flash_range_is_valid` function in the flash simulator driver contains an incorrect boundary check. The condition `(cfg->flash_size - offset) + 4 < len` allows writes to extend up to 4 bytes beyond the allocated flash memory, leading to a crash when `memcpy` or byte-by-byte writes attempt to access out-of-bounds memory.

The fix involves correcting this condition to accurately check if the requested `offset` and `len` fall within the valid range of the simulated flash memory, preventing buffer overruns. The correct check is `len > cfg->flash_size - offset`, which safely determines if the operation extends beyond the flash size without risking integer overflow.

